+**Formula:**
+The normalized correlation coefficient $C_{cor}$ between two volumes $\mathbf{y}$ and $\hat{\mathbf{y}}$ is defined as:
+$$ C_{cor}(\mathbf{y}, \hat{\mathbf{y}}) = \frac{\sum_{i} (y_i - \bar{y})(\hat{y}_i - \bar{\hat{y}})}{\sqrt{\sum_{i} (y_i - \bar{y})^2 \sum_{i} (\hat{y}_i - \bar{\hat{y}})^2}} $$
+where $y_i$ and $\hat{y}_i$ are the voxel values at index $i$, and $\bar{y}$ and $\bar{\hat{y}}$ are the mean values of the respective volumes [S1, unofficial].
